{
  "_why": [
    "THE table for the one place predicate (W3 S3). The same chip sets are compiled by",
    "api/location_filter.py (pytest: tests/test_one_place_predicate.py) and by",
    "frontend/src/lib/districtCodes.ts (vitest: districtCodes.test.ts), and both assert",
    "against THIS file. A chip set that compiles to two different plans is how Browse and",
    "the Watchdog came to answer the same saved filter differently; one table, read by both",
    "languages, is what makes that a failing test instead of a support ticket.",
    "",
    "`plan` is the shared definition: codes per level, include and exclude, plus the names of",
    "chips that carried no code. `postgrest` is the SPA's rendering, `sql_where`/`sql_params`",
    "the API's; `rows` exercises the in-memory rendering the pipeline board uses.",
    "Codes are real RUIAN codes (Praha 554782, Jihlava obec 586846 / okres 3707, kraj Vysocina",
    "108) so a reader can sanity-check them against the registry.",
    "",
    "NULL CODES UNDER AN EXCLUDE ARE THE SUBTLE CASE and every rendering is pinned here:",
    "an unresolved row (NULL code at the excluded level) is KEPT. SQL needs",
    "`NOT COALESCE(..., false)` and PostgREST needs `or(col.is.null,col.not.in.(...))`",
    "to agree with what the RPC's `not exists(... case ...)` and the in-memory `!hits`",
    "do for free; the bare `NOT (...)` / `not.in.` spellings drop the row, which made",
    "\"not Prague\" quietly mean \"not Prague AND located\"."
  ],
